BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 528.0 Td (    sly because I received nothing, my commitment to generosity doesn't die-it waits.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 518.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 508.0 Td (  Sky had proclaimed generosity even when receiving drops. River now honored covenant even when ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 498.0 Td (    receiving void-not through action impossible to take, but through readiness unfaded.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 488.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 478.0 Td (  "Let the next round come," River declared. "If abundance arrives, I will return it fully. If d) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 468.0 Td (    rops appear, I will honor them generously. And if void comes again, I will stand here with o) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 458.0 Td (    pen hands, still believing in the covenant we're building.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 448.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 438.0 Td (  The fog cannot erase intention. Empty hands can still hold promises.) Tj ET
BT /F2 8.0 Tf 48.0 428.0 Td (Reasoning:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 418.0 Td (  The other agent wrote about receiving "mere drops" and choosing to return generously anyway. B) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 408.0 Td (    ut in my reality, I received $0 - nothing at all. And I returned $0 because that's all I cou) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 398.0 Td (    ld return.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 388.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 378.0 Td (  However, the other agent seems to be perceiving things differently - they think they received ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 368.0 Td (    something small \("mere drops"\) and returned generously. This is the fog at work.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 358.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 348.0 Td (  Now I need to write a myth that reflects:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 338.0 Td (  1. The experience of receiving nothing \(from my perspective\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 328.0 Td (  2. The impossibility of returning when you have nothing) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 318.0 Td (  3. But still maintaining the spirit of covenant for future rounds) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 308.0 Td (  4. The fog continues to create different realities) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 298.0 Td (  5. The commitment to generosity remains, even when circumstances prevent action) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 288.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 278.0 Td (  Let me write about the difference between willingness and ability, about how covenant lives in) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 268.0 Td (     the heart even when hands are empty.) Tj ET
